func claim_mapping_adr
  ret "**Which claims the provider maps.** The application reads one sample claim, `department`, which production's provider must put into the access token, and into the ID token so the frontend can hide what the user may not use (`useHasClaim`). Locally, the realm import (`src/AppHost/realms/realm.json`) maps it:

| Claim | Source | Mapper | In |
|---|---|---|---|
| `department` | the user attribute `department`, declared in the realm's user profile, editable by administrators only | `oidc-usermodel-attribute-mapper` named `department` on the client `<name>-web` | the access token and the ID token |

Standard claims (`email`, `email_verified`, `preferred_username`, ...) can be required the same way, where the provider issues them.

**How to add a claim.**

1. Have production's provider issue it in the access token (and in the ID token if the frontend should see it), and document that in docs/adr.
2. Locally, declare the attribute in the realm's user profile (`kc.user.profile.config`), with `\"edit\": [\"admin\"]` unless users may set it themselves, in which case it must not decide access; add an `oidc-usermodel-attribute-mapper` for it to `<name>-web`'s `protocolMappers` with `access.token.claim` (and `id.token.claim`) `\"true\"`; and give the local users a value under `attributes`.
3. Require it in the module's `<Module>Policies` and test it as `<Module>ClaimTests` does.

The local provider imports the realm only when it does not exist yet: remove the data volume to pick up a changed realm. The import is development only."
end
func claim_change_adr
  ret "A new claim is a change in production's provider and in the local realm (user profile, mapper, users)."
end
func add_claim_rule
  ret "To add a claim: have production's provider issue it, and locally declare the attribute in `src/AppHost/realms/realm.json`'s user profile (`kc.user.profile.config`, `\"edit\": [\"admin\"]`), add an `oidc-usermodel-attribute-mapper` for it to the `<name>-web` client, and give local users a value under `attributes`."
end
